\layout Itemize

The `death rate' 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu_{k}$
\end_inset 

 has different definitions in different parts of the state space.
 
\layout Itemize

We need to consider detailed balance for each part in turn.
\layout Itemize

The Erlang delay system may be analysed as a birth-death process with birth
 rate 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda_{k}=\lambda\]

\end_inset 

 and death rate 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mu_{k}=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
k\mu & k=0,1,\dots,m-1\\
m\mu & k>m\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 


\layout ShortFoilhead


\begin_inset Formula $k\leq m$
\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

When the system's state, 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

, is less than or equal to the number of servers we have boundary flow as
 in Figure\SpecialChar ~

\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{cap:flowAtBoundaryMMma}

\end_inset 

,
