Residual Service Time
\layout Standard
\align center 

\begin_inset Graphics
	filename diagrams/residualTime.eps
	width 100text%

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

The time average of the mean residual service time can then be calculated
 in terms of the area under the curve, 
\begin_inset Formula $A(t)$
\end_inset 

.
\layout Itemize

This is given by the area under each of the triangles, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
A(t)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{M(t)}X_{i}^{2}.\]

\end_inset 

 
\layout ShortFoilhead

Residual Service Time
\layout Itemize

The average service time is the area divided by time, 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
A(t)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{M(t)}X_{i}^{2}.\]

\end_inset 

 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\frac{A(t)}{t} & = & \frac{M(t)}{t}\frac{A(t)}{M(t)}\\
 & = & \frac{1}{2}\frac{M(t)}{t}\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{M(t)}X_{i}^{2}}{M(t)}.\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 
\begin_deeper 
\layout Itemize

we have introduced the number of arrivals after time 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset 

, as 
\begin_inset Formula $M\left(t\right)$
\end_inset 

.
 
\layout Itemize

As 
\begin_inset Formula $t\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset 

, 
\emph on 
if the variance is finite
\emph default 
, we find that 
\begin_inset Formula $M(t)\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset 

 and we obtain
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{R}=\frac{1}{2}\lambda\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle .\]

\end_inset 

 
\end_deeper 
\layout ShortFoilhead

Pollaczek-Khinchin Formula
\layout Itemize

Again assuming that time averages and ensemble averages are equal we substitute
 back into (
\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{eqn:arrivals}

\end_inset 

) to obtain the Pollaczek-Khinchin formula 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{W}=\frac{\lambda\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle }{2(1-\rho)}.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

This implies that the total waiting time in the system is 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{T}=\bar{X}+\frac{\lambda\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle }{2(1-\rho)}\]

\end_inset 

 and through Little's formula we can obtain the expected queue length, 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{N}_{Q}$
\end_inset 

, and the expected number in the system, 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{N}$
\end_inset 

.
 
\layout ShortFoilhead

Sanity Check --- Markov Service times
\layout Itemize

The exponentially distributed service times, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(X\right)=\mu\exp\left(-\mu X\right),\]

\end_inset 

have a mean of 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{X}=\frac{1}{\mu}\]

\end_inset 

 and a variance of 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{1}{\mu^{2}}$
\end_inset 

 leading to a second moment
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\frac{2}{\mu^{2}}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

Substituting into the Pollaczek-Khinchin formula we obtain 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\bar{W} & = & \frac{\rho}{\mu\left(1-\rho\right)}\\
 & = & \frac{\rho}{\mu-\lambda}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

which is identical to those we derived for the 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1$
\end_inset 

 queue.
\layout ShortFoilhead

Deterministic Service --- 
\begin_inset Formula $M/D/1$
\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

Some systems have deterministic service times.
 For example, transmission of fixed length packets over a channel with a
 fixed bandwidth.
 
\layout Itemize

We represent a `deterministic distribution' as
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(X\right)=\delta\left(X-\frac{1}{\mu}\right)\]

\end_inset 

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta\left(\cdot\right)$
\end_inset 

is the Dirac delta function.
 
\layout Itemize

For this system 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle X\right\rangle =\frac{1}{\mu}\]

\end_inset 

and 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\frac{1}{\mu^{2}}\]

\end_inset 


\emph on 
i.e.

\emph default 
 the variance is zero.
 
\layout ShortFoilhead

P-K Formula for Deterministic Systems
\layout Itemize

For this system 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle X\right\rangle =\frac{1}{\mu}\]

\end_inset 

and 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\frac{1}{\mu^{2}}\]

\end_inset 


\emph on 
i.e.

\emph default 
 the variance is zero.
 
\layout Itemize

Substituting into the Pollaczek-Khinchin formula we obtain 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{W}=\frac{\rho}{2\mu\left(1-\rho\right)}.\]

\end_inset 


